# Review routing for release-critical paths.
#
# There is deliberately no global `*` rule — ordinary feature work does not
# need to wait on one person. These are the files where a mistake is either
# expensive to unwind (the release process, migrations) or changes how the
# repository itself behaves (CI, rulesets, contributor docs).
#
# CODEOWNERS only *requests* a review. To make it blocking, tick
# "Require review from Code Owners" in the `dev` ruleset.

# Release process, versioning, and the changelog that feeds the GitHub release.
/docs/RELEASING.md      @MonoliYoda
/package.json           @MonoliYoda
/CHANGELOG.md           @MonoliYoda

# CI, templates, and anything else that changes repository behaviour.
/.github/               @MonoliYoda

# Migrations apply once and in order; a bad one is not a revert away.
/src/db/migrations/     @MonoliYoda

# The working agreements themselves.
/CONTRIBUTING.md        @MonoliYoda
/CLAUDE.md              @MonoliYoda
